- Story & Context: When the relief icebreaker finally arrived at the abandoned Sørkapp light to end the winter watch, the boarding party discovered the beacon unmanned, greeted only by the rich, warm odor of coconut oil that had been rubbed into every inch of the radio gear to prevent sea-salt seizure. Rigged to a windmill generator, an automated tape loop was endlessly cycling an ecstatic, sun-soaked anthem where chiming glockenspiels and a roaring acid bassline pulsed in perfect 124 BPM synchronization with the flashing lighthouse beam. Written on the galley chalkboard beside a stack of empty tin cans was the keeper's final transmission hook: "We set the table on the open water!" Below the cliffs, a pod of migrating white belugas drifted through the slush, surfacing in rhythm with the high-wattage tropical broadcast echoing over the frozen sea.
